insert into public.passages (id, code, skill_id, sat_alignment, grade_band, title, body, status)
values ('01da2e99-0526-5bce-96ed-454544918009', 'wg9-argument-writing-p01', (select id from public.skills where slug = 'write-g9-argument-writing'), null,
        '9-12', $q$Bird-Safe Windows at Hollis High$q$, $q$(1) The new science wing at Hollis High School has a wall of tall glass windows facing the wooded hill behind the track. (2) Since the wing opened last fall, the custodial staff have found more than sixty dead or stunned birds beneath that wall. (3) Birds are interesting animals that live almost everywhere on Earth. (4) Birds cannot see clear or reflective glass, so they fly toward the trees they see reflected in it. (5) A student survey team counted strikes for six weeks and found that nearly all of them happened along the same forty feet of glass.

(6) Some teachers worry that patterned window film would block the view and darken the classrooms. (7) This is a fair concern, since the view of the hill is one of the wing's best features. (8) However, the recommended film uses small white dots spaced two inches apart, which leaves more than ninety percent of the glass clear. (9) At the Brindle Nature Center, a similar film reduced bird strikes by about eighty percent in its first year, and staff said visitors rarely noticed the dots.

(10) The film would cost about $900 for the forty feet of glass where most strikes occur. (11) The Hollis Environmental Club has already raised $400 toward that cost with a spring plant sale. (12) Installing the film would give biology classes a chance to keep counting strikes and measure whether the change worked. (13) Anyway, birds are cool and the school should probably do something about it someday.$q$, 'draft')
