insert into public.passages (id, code, skill_id, sat_alignment, grade_band, title, body, status)
values ('7b7dcb20-0bef-591b-885d-d40867279794', 'wg9-argument-writing-p02', (select id from public.skills where slug = 'write-g9-argument-writing'), null,
        '9-12', $q$Keyboarding for Ninth Graders$q$, $q$(1) At Marlowe High School, students type almost every major assignment, from lab reports to history essays. (2) Yet most ninth graders have never been taught to type, and many still search for each key using two fingers. (3) Marlowe should add a six-week keyboarding unit to the ninth-grade technology course. (4) Last spring, the technology teacher, Ms. Okafor, timed eighty ninth graders and found an average speed of only eighteen words per minute. (5) Students who had taken a typing class in middle school averaged forty-one words per minute. (6) Slow typing is a total pain on timed writing tests, where kids run out of time before they get their ideas down.

(7) Some students argue that typing lessons are unnecessary because they can simply speak into their devices and let software type for them. (8) Voice typing is certainly useful for homework at home. (9) It is not allowed during most school tests, though, and it would not work well in a crowded classroom where thirty students would be talking at once.

(10) A keyboarding unit would not require new equipment, since every classroom already has a laptop cart. (11) Free typing practice programs are available online, and Ms. Okafor has offered to design the lessons herself. (12) My cousin types really fast because she plays a lot of computer games. (13) For these reasons, a short keyboarding unit is a low-cost way to help ninth graders work faster and show what they know.$q$, 'draft')
