insert into public.passages (id, code, skill_id, sat_alignment, grade_band, title, body, status)
values ('b643b1e3-f9c4-5906-84b2-ce90f12f9dca', 'wg9-argument-writing-p03', (select id from public.skills where slug = 'write-g9-argument-writing'), null,
        '9-12', $q$The Kessler Park Bandstand$q$, $q$(1) In the center of Kessler Park stands a wooden bandstand built in 1912, where town bands once played concerts every Sunday in summer. (2) Today its paint is peeling, two of its steps are cracked, and the town has fenced it off. (3) The bandstand is old. (4) A report by the county historical society lists it as the last bandstand of its kind in the county. (5) Older residents remember dancing there, and photographs in the town library show crowds of hundreds gathered on the lawn around it.

(6) Some council members argue that the town should tear down the bandstand and build a modern stage. (7) They point out that repairing the old structure would cost about $38,000. (8) A new stage, however, would cost nearly twice as much, according to estimates in the same council report. (9) Tearing down the bandstand would also erase a piece of local history that could never be rebuilt.

(10) A restored bandstand could serve the whole community again. (11) The Kessler High jazz band, the community choir and the library's summer story hour have all said they would hold events there. (12) Shops near the park have reported that their sales rise on evenings when the park hosts events. (13) So that is my opinion about the bandstand.$q$, 'draft')
