insert into public.passages (id, code, skill_id, sat_alignment, grade_band, title, body, status)
values ('f54c81d7-40db-5110-8d07-8ec5413721fd', 'wg9-argument-writing-p04', (select id from public.skills where slug = 'write-g9-argument-writing'), null,
        '9-12', $q$A Climbing Wall for Brenford High$q$, $q$(1) Brenford High School's physical education program offers mostly team sports such as basketball, volleyball and flag football. (2) Students who do not enjoy competitive games often sit on the bleachers and do as little as possible. (3) Brenford should build an indoor climbing wall in the old auxiliary gym. (4) Climbing builds strength, balance and problem-solving skills, and students can progress at their own pace instead of competing against a team. (5) At Ridley Falls High, which added a wall three years ago, the share of students who said they enjoyed gym class rose from 48 percent to 70 percent. (6) Climbing is also fun.

(7) Parents may worry that climbing is dangerous. (8) That worry is understandable when people picture climbers high on a rocky cliff. (9) A school wall, however, would be only twelve feet high, students would wear harnesses, and every climb would be supervised by a certified teacher. (10) Ridley Falls has reported no serious injuries on its wall since it opened.

(11) The wall would cost about $15,000 to build and install. (12) A state fitness grant pays up to $10,000 for new physical education equipment, and the athletic boosters have offered to raise the rest.$q$, 'draft')
