   $q$How does sentence (9) respond to the board's concern in sentence (8)?$q$, $q$[{"text":"It agrees that the orchard should be cleared for parking.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"confuses-concession-with-reversal"},{"text":"It accepts that the problem exists but shows it is limited to a few days.","is_correct":true},{"text":"It offers evidence that visitors enjoy parking along the road.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"unsupported-inference"},{"text":"It claims the board is wrong and that the lot never fills up.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"misreads-concession"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$It accepts that the problem exists but shows it is limited to a few days.$q$, $q$Sentence (9) says the problem is real, then narrows it to about six weekends a year, which makes clearing the orchard seem out of proportion. The writer never says the lot does not fill up.$q$, 'draft', 'c02e7959-c79e-51f0-b3d8-c97d30e469cc')
