   $q$Which revision of sentence (7) states the opposing claim most clearly and fairly?$q$, $q$[{"text":"Some people argue that students should simply walk home instead.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"mismatched-counterclaim"},{"text":"Everyone knows that free passes would cost far too much money.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"overgeneralization"},{"text":"Some people think city buses are bad and that nobody should ride them.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"vague-counterclaim"},{"text":"Some school board members argue that free passes would cost more than the district can afford.","is_correct":true}]$q$::jsonb, $q$Some school board members argue that free passes would cost more than the district can afford.$q$, $q$The writer's response in sentences (8) through (10) is about cost, so the opposing claim must be about affordability. The suggestion that students walk home is a different objection that the paragraph never answers.$q$, 'draft', '25e5d099-6c79-527b-ae98-20202416c70a')
